 "note": "StudyE9b's alarm, dismiss and trigger thresholds are score QUANTILES of the pooled negative instants, so under ONE per-tier affine map with a > 0 a quantile maps to the transformed quantile and every decision, every episode and every invocation count is identical: only the delivered VALUES move onto a common scale. Under the CROSS-FITTED calibration that is no longer true, because the pooled negatives carry five different maps, so a pooled quantile is not the image of the raw quantile and the decisions move too. The invocation counts for all three scales are reported so this can be checked rather than asserted, and the one-map row is the clean statement of what the calibration alone does to the measured capture.",
